  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_9' aria-label=\" Rohit Kochhar versus Vipul Infrastructure Developers Ltd. & Ors. pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('9','2024','2024_11_1289_1311','2024INSC920'); ><font size='4'> <strong>ROHIT KOCHHAR<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>VIPUL INFRASTRUCTURE DEVELOPERS LTD. & ORS. </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2024] 11 S.C.R. 1289</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2024 INSC 920</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010006992024></button></font><br><strong>Coram : J.B. PARDIWALA, R MAHADEVAN</strong><br> Issue for Consideration Whether the relief sought by the plaintiff in respect to the suit property can be entirely obtained through the personal obedience of the defendants warranting the application of the proviso to Section 16 of the Code of Civil Procedure, 1908 &ndash; Proviso to s.16 &ndash; When not applicable &ndash; Suit for specific performance of the contract in respect of the suit property situated in Gurugram, filed in the Delhi High Court &ndash; Single Judge held that the suit was maintainable in view of proviso to s.16<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 26-11-2024</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> SPECIAL LEAVE PETITION (CIVIL) No. 10169/2008</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Dismissed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('9','2024','2024_11_1289_1311','2024INSC920','S')><i <i class='fas fa-columns me-2'></i>Split view</a></div><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' onclick=open_splitview('9','2024','2024_11_1289_1311